From 6878e82a9ccc19e7badb057591aa6679b46eaadb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JeyKul <jey@kulovac.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:08:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] serial: qcom-geni: handle interrupts while the port is
 suspending

uart_suspend_port() sets uport->suspended, waits up to 30 ms for the
transmitter and only then calls shutdown(), which disables the IRQ. An
interrupt in that window (on the Tab S7+ the QCA6390 answering the IBS
sleep request hci_qca sends at suspend) was answered with IRQ_NONE and
never cleared. The line is level triggered, so it fired until the core
gave up with "irq nobody cared" and disabled it for good: every later
Bluetooth command timed out until reboot.

Only bail out once the SE is runtime suspended (clocks off); before that,
handle the interrupt as usual so its source is drained.

Tested: 40 RTC-woken suspends with Bluetooth on. Before: ~200k IRQs,
IRQ 164 disabled, BT dead. After: ~3.6k IRQs, BT off/on works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
index a851b8f0e..216d2ef68 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -1211,7 +1211,14 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_geni_serial_isr(int isr, void *dev)
 	struct tty_port *tport = &uport->state->port;
 	struct qcom_geni_serial_port *port = to_dev_port(uport);
 
-	if (uport->suspended)
+	/*
+	 * uart_suspend_port() marks the port suspended before shutdown()
+	 * disables the IRQ. The line is level triggered: an event in that
+	 * window (e.g. a Bluetooth controller acking a sleep request) must
+	 * be handled, or it fires until the core disables the IRQ for good.
+	 * Only skip it once the SE is powered down.
+	 */
+	if (uport->suspended && pm_runtime_status_suspended(uport->dev))
 		return IRQ_NONE;
 
 	uart_port_lock(uport);
-- 
2.56.0

